(Discrepancy 3 — RESOLVED, 2026-08-22, vox #66. On 0.4.9 and earlier, a
 top-level TEXT global PRINTED from inside a function defined EARLIER in
 the file rendered a raw pointer instead of the text. The value itself
 was intact: assigning it to a local first and printing the local was
 correct, and so was a comparison against the literal. Only the
 print/format path was wrong, and only for a text (a number global was
 fine). Moving the function definition below the declaration used to fix
 it, but as of 0.4.10 that is no longer necessary.
 LANGUAGE.md:757 says top-level variables "can be used inside functions",
 now with the ordering rule stated explicitly; LANGUAGE.md:3400 leans on
 that same promise for branch-declared names ("exactly like a top-level
 declaration" — which it now is, correctly, so FMT-42 holds without a
 caveat). Reached from this section via FMT-42, but the defect belonged
 to Functions / Variables, not here — see `functions.md` Discrepancy 1.
 Written as comparisons rather than raw prints because the address,
 though stable within one build, is not something to pin in a ledger.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox probe.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   top level printed the text
   the local copy printed the text
   the comparison inside the function succeeded
   the direct print inside the function printed the text
)
To 'show label'.
  a text called copied is label.
  If copied is equal to "one" then, Print "the local copy printed the text". Otherwise, Print "the local copy did NOT print the text".
  If label is equal to "one" then, Print "the comparison inside the function succeeded". Otherwise, Print "the comparison inside the function FAILED".
  a text called printed is "{label}".
  If printed is equal to "one" then, Print "the direct print inside the function printed the text". Otherwise, Print "the direct print inside the function did NOT print the text".

a text called label is "one".
If label is equal to "one" then, Print "top level printed the text". Otherwise, Print "top level did NOT print the text".
'show label'.
